  "passage": {
    "title": "Living in a Tiny House",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "In recent years, a new type of home has become popular in many countries: the tiny house. These houses are usually between fifteen and forty square metres, which is smaller than many hotel rooms. Some are built on wheels so that the owners can move them, while others stand on a fixed base."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "People choose tiny houses for several reasons. The most common one is money. A normal family house may cost hundreds of thousands of pounds, but a tiny house can cost as little as thirty thousand. Smaller homes also cost less to heat and to clean. For people who want to own a home without a large mortgage, this is very attractive."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Others are interested in the lifestyle. Living in a small space means owning fewer things. Sarah Jones, who lives in a tiny house in Wales, says she sold two-thirds of her belongings before moving in. At first it was hard, she says, but now she spends less time tidying and more time outside. Many tiny-house owners say they feel less stressed and have more time for friends."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Of course, there are problems. Space is limited, so visitors cannot stay overnight, and it can be difficult to live with a partner or children. In many places the law does not allow people to park a tiny house wherever they like, and finding a legal place to live can take months. Storage is another challenge: a tiny house has no room for a bicycle, a large fridge, or a big family dinner."
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Even so, interest keeps growing. Television programmes about tiny houses are popular, and some towns have created special areas where owners can rent a small piece of land. Experts say tiny houses will not replace normal homes, but they could be a useful option for students, older people and anyone who wants a simpler life."
      }
    ]
  },
